      "writtenOn": "2026-03-12T17:33:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the better fix would be to make this iterate over the instructions for a single entry point. This is going to have the same issue for Print where a call in an unused entrypoint would trigger an error incorrectly.\n\nMy prefernece would be to keep the get/has Resources checks in here and make the instruction walk smarter (we probably have similar issues in other CanGenerate checks.)",
      "revId": "dc3a7344d657bc620c7d8873f77398630afdca6a",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4a1a9262_82377ec9",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/spirv/writer/writer.cc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 122,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002241
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-12T23:47:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We very likely do have issues like this, which is why I\u0027m keen to remove these checks from `CanGenerate()`. It makes a lot more sense to me to put the checks next to (or in) the code that they are protecting. Making `CanGenerate()` do more complicated checks here feels unappealing when we already have the information we want to check in the transform that consumes it.\n\nSee https://dawn-review.googlesource.com/c/dawn/+/283697 for another example where we moved validation from `CanGenerate()` to the relevant transform, to avoid duplicating logic between the two places.\n\nCan you explain your concern about `Print()`? By the time we get to `Print()` there is exactly one entry point, so there shouldn\u0027t be any problems there?",
      "parentUuid": "e6caf5bf_a5c21d6f",
      "revId": "dc3a7344d657bc620c7d8873f77398630afdca6a",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "43f64199_8618da7f",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/spirv/writer/writer.cc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 122,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000257
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-13T03:02:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "On line 128, we check if `Print` is used in _any_ instruction. This means, if I have a `dbg_shader` and a `rel_shader` switching between them would still trigger a can generate error because this code doesn\u0027t respect the selected entry point.\n\nSo, the same issue getResource and hasResource encounter, a non-ep shader causing a generate error in the current entry point, would trigger for Print, and any of the CanGenerate methods were we check for specific method usages.",
      "parentUuid": "4a1a9262_82377ec9",
      "revId": "dc3a7344d657bc620c7d8873f77398630afdca6a",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
